From 86eea94ed6fe4ab9f4c181d6f530cf6846a978aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 06:07:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 70/76] perf(sumcheck): back partially evaluated tables on the
 folded support only

The partially evaluated multivariates were allocated over [0, ceil(end/2)) for every polynomial,
also for selectors and other columns whose backed range starts deep inside the trace. Back them on
[floor(start/2), ceil(end/2)) instead, and move the backed range down in place on later rounds
(Polynomial::rebase_backed_range), so the tables never hold the leading virtual zeroes.
